<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Podlachia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Podlasie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Podlasie is a historical region in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, centred on Białystok and bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>. It formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin">Union of Lublin</a> in 1569 transferred it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-of-the-kingdom-of-poland">Crown of Poland</a>. Its mixed Polish, Belarusian, Lithuanian, Jewish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> population made it a meeting point of Catholic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> traditions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/podlachia.jpg" alt="Podlachia" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marek Mróz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2019-07_Tykocin_(9).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>At the Union of Lublin in 1569 King Sigismund II Augustus transferred <b>Podlasie</b>, Volhynia, Kiev and Bracław to the Crown of Poland, and the grand duchy entered the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth with a common monarch, diet and foreign policy but its own army, treasury, offices and law.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>This gave the Polish nobility the leverage to insist on terms favourable to the Crown, including the transfer of <b>Podlachia</b>, Volhynia and the large Ukrainian palatinates of Kiev and Bracław from Lithuanian to Polish administration.</blockquote><a href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
